      "LUCY: - so I saw first-hand how the hospitality industry brings infrastructure to communities that really need it. But I also saw the problems tha…\nLUCY: Not try to prevent progress, but convince developers there are benefits to being sustainable and community oriented.\nTUTOR: Why not think big?\nLUCY: Absolutely. In return, the labour force would be more consistent and better trained and more motivated. Win-win.",
      "PRAMA: Hi! Come in, come in -\nLUCY: Wow, something smells amazing!",
      "LUCY: Okay, I say flashlight - - you say -\nANNIKA: Lampe de poche.\nLUCY: You say -",
      "ANNIKA: Taxi.\nLUCY: See? It’s the same in every language.",
      "PRAMA: You must have been freaking. Howrah Station’s enormous! I went through on pilgrimage to Puri - I missed my connection twice.\nLUCY: And you couldn’t speak Bengali?"
    ]
  },
